o make that decision about whether to  send their child back to school  in the area where they live they should  rely on the public health  recommendations for their local area  they should look to see what mitigation  strategies their school is taking  they should take stock of their own  personal situation the decision to send  your child back to school or not  is a luxury that not every parent has  yeah and good luck trying to get kids to  socially distance tara when they  when they haven't seen their friends in  a very long time so  parents are very nervous rightfully so  what's your advice for their parents  every single parent i know gail is  asking me the same question and really  it boils down to those things that you  heard in the piece  what is the community transmission in  your area you should be aware of it are  you in a zone where  it's safe to reopen the schools also you  want to know what is your school doing  so parents should feel empowered to talk  to their school and find out what kinds  of mitigation strategies they're putting  in place  is your child a vulnerable child talk to  your pediatrician and see if they have  any concerns about your child going back  to school  and then as a parent obviously you can  do things like packing extra masks hand  sanitizer but i think one of the  important things we don't often talk  about  is just talking to our kids they're  going to be going back to something that  isn't what they're used to  they may have their own anxieties and  fears and you really want to sit down  with them and have an  honest conversation in a calm reassuring  way  where you listen to them and their  concerns and you walk them through what  to expect  yeah they take their cues from you you  got to be reassuring during these times  thank you very much tara
 

